// Which shorts project each published video was made in.
//
// Hand-written, never inferred. Titles changed between production and
// publication, so a title match that looks right can be wrong -- the
// failure this project exists to avoid. Read by `atlas-ingest videos`.
//
// Keys are video URLs as a blog post declares them (any form that post
// uses; they are compared by video id). Values are directories under
// ~/github/softwarewrighter/shorts/projects/. Five ML Concepts episodes are
// NOT listed here: episode N maps to 5MLC-N (episode 1 to daily5-20260203)
// by a rule in crates/atlas-video/src/episodes.rs.
//
// Every row below is Provenance::Declared: the repository owner confirmed
// it. The comment on each row is the evidence the pair was drafted from on
// 2026-09-22, kept so a later reader can see what it rested on -- but the
// row is in the corpus because the owner said yes, not because the
// evidence looked convincing. Videos absent from this file have no known
// shorts project (most long-form videos were never shorts) and keep an
// empty script until their text arrives; see docs/video-sources.md.
JoinMap(
    confirmed: {
        // Recorded in docs/video-sources.md.
        // "976 parameters is more than billions?!"
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/O6U06cGkKc4": "trm",
        // "AI in Your Pocket"
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/fyEuH1BprLI": "pocket-llm",
        // "Given enough eyeballs..."
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/KgtiBy4rdm4": "many-eyes-learning",

        // Confirmed by the owner on 2026-09-22.
        // "ML Frontier 1: Neural Collapse"; description opens "ML Frontier
        // 01 - Neural Collapse".
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ElFwTSuHjnM": "MLF-01",
        // "ML Frontier 2: ICRL"; description opens "ML Frontier Episode 2
        // - In-Context Reinforcement Learning".
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/D4KrvmqOwEY": "MLF-02a",
        // "ML Frontier 3: Structure Beats Scale"; commit "Add MLF-03a
        // Structure Beats Scale YouTube Short".
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/6MluFFCb1cA": "MLF-03a",
        // "ML Frontier 4: Is Chain of Thought Real?"; description opens
        // with the same title.
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/mBLFTyh1EKk": "MLF-04",
        // "XSkill: A Memory Layer for Multimodal Agents"; description
        // opens with the same title.
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/QelUyffoo1g": "xskill",
        // "Trash Talkin' Tic Tac Toe"; commit "Add Game MCP PoC YouTube
        // Short (Trash Talkin' Tic Tac Toe)".
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/n_NFFLCtj_M": "game-mcp-poc",
        // "DeepSeek's Engram Paper Tested on Mac"; description names
        // DeepSeek's Engram paper, and the project is the MLX one.
        "https://youtube.com/shorts/aGoQHs6S1nk": "engram-poc-mlx",
        // "Engram PoC: Now With CUDA Power"; description opens "ENGRAM
        // Part 2: Now on NVIDIA CUDA with Unsloth."
        "https://youtube.com/shorts/uvbfu0WKa3A": "engram-poc-unsloth",
        // "Sinkhorn on Blackwell (mHC part 2)"; description opens "mHC
        // goes CUDA. Phase 2 complete."
        "https://youtube.com/shorts/BOuBFn5e1gA": "mHC-cuda",
        // "JSON or Something Better?"; description opens "JSON is
        // everywhere - but it's not the only option."
        "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/3ezjk1CnZEU": "json-et-al",
        // "Learning More About In-Context Learning"; description opens on
